</spork>

The problem with having more easily accessible sources of Pw recharge is
that mana is supposed to be a finite resource; with too many sources, it
become effectively infinite.  

Right now, spellcasting is so good in Nethack that it's well worth the 
effort for any role to bolt on a robe and hat of smart, just for the 
high-utility tricks available in spell form; the only difference between
these classes and wizards/priests after this becomes the lack of a huge
Pw reservoir.  With more transient Pw recharge, the class differentiation 
becomes even smaller than it currently is.

Right now in vanilla, anyone who can be neutral and wish up the Eye of
Mumble is almost as good as a wizard -- skill levels don't matter except
for those few spells that you want to cast right on the first try (like
finger of death), and the recharge is so strong that even a teeny-teeny
reservoir fills up to 25 or 30 points in a few turns.

